{"id": "AEC-R10", "version": 2, "type": "requirement", "subject": "aec-scope", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "A snapshot names exactly what it describes (commit, or dirty working tree, and the extraction method), and two snapshots are compared only when their methods match, against the merge base for a PR (spec 005, WP1A). Not yet implemented; Zach's clarifications are recorded in the spec (PR #24, 2026-11-01)", "rationale": "Zach approved the WP1A package in Claude chat 2026-10-30 20:29 CT; anchored to the spec status line that records it.", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-P0@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-R2@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R5@1"}, {"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R10@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "specs/005-commit-snapshots/spec.md", "sha256": "1c2c74536c1d594a3c93125a40630c7e09d7c60041640d75a58810c32436693a", "locator": "q:a snapshot names exactly what it describes", "for": "text"}, {"path": "specs/005-commit-snapshots/spec.md", "sha256": "1c2c74536c1d594a3c93125a40630c7e09d7c60041640d75a58810c32436693a", "locator": "q:I approve WP1A.", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "DEC-023", "version": 1, "type": "decision", "status": "accepted", "decided_by": "AU-zach", "subject": "aec-scope", "origin": "projection", "canonical": "relay-kit-private governance/decisions.jsonl DEC-023", "text": "Bring AEC to a first public release that can build momentum: the readiness changes claude:aec outlined (README front door, CONTRIBUTING, packaging fixes, CI matrix, legacy labelling, scoped first issues, tagged release), a true and realized value add, and hygiene enough for 'a release that we can be proud of', coordinating across the Claude, Codex and ChatGPT threads.", "rationale": "Owner decision: \"Work with this thread [...00324d1a] And other coordinating threads from Claude, Codex, and ChatGPT to bring the project up to where the inclusion could build momentum, including the various changes you outlined above, a true and realized value add, and hygiene enough for a release that we can be proud of.\" (11:05 CT), after claude:aec's list of must-haves, contributor work and value evidence (10:59 CT)", "anchors": [{"root": "relay-kit-private", "path": "governance/decisions.jsonl", "sha256": "a333466e051c398bb31b49de86daa2ff01414ad7ef97a1b556c1a530cc0276ef", "locator": "q:\"id\": \"DEC-023\"", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "DEC-024", "version": 1, "type": "decision", "status": "accepted", "decided_by": "AU-zach", "subject": "aec-scope", "origin": "projection", "canonical": "relay-kit-private governance/decisions.jsonl DEC-024", "text": "Run the probe-001 pilot (18 trials, Data-Guide@0607401) before WP1A, after repairing and freezing the pre-registration per Kate's review; this changes the WP2-probe-after-WP1A order for this pilot only.", "rationale": "Owner decision: Selected \"Run pilot now (Recommended)\" in answer to claude:aec's question: \"Run the 18-trial pilot on Data-Guide now, before WP1A? It costs roughly a few hundred thousand Sonnet tokens.\" Options offered: run now / freeze and run after WP1A / smaller pilot now.", "anchors": [{"root": "relay-kit-private", "path": "governance/decisions.jsonl", "sha256": "a333466e051c398bb31b49de86daa2ff01414ad7ef97a1b556c1a530cc0276ef", "locator": "q:\"id\": \"DEC-024\"", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "DEC-025", "version": 1, "type": "decision", "status": "accepted", "decided_by": "AU-zach", "subject": "aec-scope", "origin": "projection", "canonical": "relay-kit-private governance/decisions.jsonl DEC-025", "text": "Stop committing the generated edge snapshot: aec init git-ignores .aec/edges.jsonl in adopters' repos and AEC untracks its own (v0.4.1, AEC PR #26). Condition: later revisit whether the implementation and use of edges match the purpose stated for them, and the owner investigates what is currently going on with that idea.", "rationale": "Owner decision: \"Alright. I'll agree with that, with the stipulation that we later revisit that the implementation and use of edges be compared with the purpose stated for it and I investigate what is currently actually going on with that idea\" (13:41 CT), answering claude:aec-release's recommendation to untrack the snapshot (13:39 CT)", "anchors": [{"root": "relay-kit-private", "path": "governance/decisions.jsonl", "sha256": "a333466e051c398bb31b49de86daa2ff01414ad7ef97a1b556c1a530cc0276ef", "locator": "q:\"id\": \"DEC-025\"", "for": "text"}]}
