{"id": "AMB-adopted-by-others", "version": 1, "type": "ambition", "subject": "aec-scope", "owner": "zach", "text": "Others find AEC useful.", "quote": "my ambition (ambition should be a record type, like decision) is for others to find it useful.", "origin": "Zach, Claude chat 83a9f59e, 2026-11-01 21:19 CT", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-P0@1"}]}
{"id": "AMB-tiered-agents", "version": 1, "type": "ambition", "subject": "aec-scope", "owner": "zach", "text": "Tiered agentic development: an architectural or coordinating agent works from the edge snapshot, and is deliberately denied module- and function-level detail held elsewhere in the agent network, keeping some of the gains of asymmetric information. It may first run as an experiment.", "quote": "Edge snapshots will eventually be for a tiered approach to agentic development, where an architectural agent or coordinator can look at that, but that additional information is counterbalanced by deliberately not having access to the module level and function level information outside of other parts of the agent network, preserving some of the gains of asymmetry, and that might also end up as an experiment.", "origin": "Zach, Claude chat 83a9f59e, 2026-11-02 08:36 CT", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-P0@1"}]}
{"id": "AMB-radical-restructuring", "version": 1, "type": "ambition", "subject": "aec-scope", "owner": "zach", "text": "Support radical change: refactoring or completely restructuring a project while still fulfilling the commitments and purposes set out earlier.", "quote": "another part of AEC, is the support for radical change and radical refactoring to something and complete restructuring that still fulfills the commitments and purposes set out earlier. That's otherwise, as far as I understand it, very difficult.", "origin": "Zach, Claude chat 83a9f59e, 2026-11-02 08:45 CT", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-P0@1"}]}
{"id": "AMB-owner-reporting", "version": 1, "type": "ambition", "subject": "aec-scope", "owner": "zach", "text": "A reporting layer, in AEC or beside it, that makes the owner's part (keeping up with PRs, decisions, ambitions) quicker, easier and less mistake-prone, alongside the agentic parts.", "quote": "I'm already finding it somewhat of a struggle to keep up with the PRs, the decisions, the ambitions, things like that. There needs to be a reporting layer. It may or may not be built in AEC itself, but in addition to like the telemetry, eventually there needs to be some stuff to make my part of this quicker and easier and less mistake prone, as well as the agentic bits.", "origin": "Zach, Claude chat 83a9f59e, 2026-11-02 08:45 CT", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-P0@1"}]}
{"id": "AMB-multi-tier-humans", "version": 1, "type": "ambition", "subject": "aec-scope", "owner": "zach", "text": "Coordinate AEC work across human development teams: deciders, plus non-directing humans who evaluate, support or are affiliated with the project and may run their own agent networks.", "quote": "eventually, yeah, we're going to be coordinating probably deciders, independent or non-deciding or non-directing, okay, that's a better way, non-directing humans who evaluate or support or otherwise are affiliated with the project and might also run their own agents. That will be an interesting layer of complexity. Multi-tiered agents, multi-tiered humans with multiple agent networks.", "origin": "Zach, Claude chat 83a9f59e, 2026-11-02 08:45 CT", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-P0@1"}]}
