{"id": "CL-R11-hygiene", "version": 1, "type": "claim", "tier": "candidate", "claim_category": "requirement_satisfaction", "subject": "aec-scope", "text": "check and source show report an anchor whose file grew by appending, with the anchored bytes intact as its prefix, as `appended` and not as a finding; an edited or truncated prefix stays mismatch; whole-file anchors outside append_only are unchanged; an exact duplicate record line loads once with a duplicate-line warning, a differing one stays the unique error", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R11@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "code:src.aec.sources.anchored_prefix"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "code:src.aec.sources.SourceContext.inspect"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "code:src.aec.records.Store.load"}]}
{"id": "EV-R11-hygiene-tests", "version": 1, "type": "evidence", "tier": "candidate", "evidence_kind": "contract_conformance", "method": "tests.test_ledger_hygiene (12 anchor fixture cases from tests/fixtures/anchors/appended.json, 3 duplicate-line fixtures in tests/fixtures/duplicates/), committed failing before the implementation (14 of 20 failing at 2a7ead4); full suite; aec check on .aec/records.jsonl before and after; 2026-11-04", "limits": "integrity of a prefix only: `appended` says nothing about whether bytes appended later supersede or contradict the anchored passage; append_only is a declaration by whoever configures the repository, not an observation that the file is append-only; prefixes are searched only at newline boundaries", "text": "all fixture cases yield their expected state; decoys (unchanged file, undeclared grown file, reformatted or conflicting duplicates) are not relaxed; own records go from 13 anchor warnings to 3 real mismatches with 0 errors", "relations": [{"rel": "supports", "to": "CL-R11-hygiene@1"}, {"rel": "observed_on", "to": "code:src.aec.sources.anchored_prefix"}, {"rel": "observed_on", "to": "code:src.aec.records.Store.load"}]}
{"id": "EV-R11-hygiene-tests", "version": 2, "type": "evidence", "tier": "candidate", "evidence_kind": "contract_conformance", "method": "tests.test_ledger_hygiene after the DEC-038 fix round on PR #48 (reviews by Kate and review:claude-fresh, 2026-11-04): added failing-first tests committed at a53618c (6 failing, 11 passing): whitespace/CRLF duplicate variants (tests/fixtures/duplicates/trailing-space.jsonl; CRLF and leading-space built in the test) with byte-identical decoys, an explicit prefix_bytes ending mid-line followed by growth of that line with newline-ended and unchanged-file decoys, and the supersession wording of the appended note; full suite; aec check on .aec/records.jsonl; 2026-11-04", "limits": "integrity of a prefix only: `appended` says nothing about whether bytes appended later supersede or contradict the anchored passage (the note now says a later entry may supersede it; no scan of the appended bytes); append_only is a declaration by whoever configures the repository, not an observation that the file is append-only, and applies per root alias; a proper prefix must end at a newline, for prefix_bytes and declared files alike; duplicate lines are compared as written (split on LF only)", "text": "all fixture cases yield their expected state, including the fix-round cases: duplicate copies differing only in surrounding whitespace or CRLF are the `unique` error while byte-identical copies stay the duplicate-line warning; growth after a mid-line prefix_bytes prefix is mismatch while a newline-ended prefix is appended; own records still show 0 errors and the 3 real anchor mismatches", "relations": [{"rel": "supports", "to": "CL-R11-hygiene@1"}, {"rel": "observed_on", "to": "code:src.aec.sources.anchored_prefix"}, {"rel": "observed_on", "to": "code:src.aec.records.Store.load"}, {"rel": "supersedes", "to": "EV-R11-hygiene-tests@1"}]}
