// 2026-11-04 records/purpose-p0v2 (claude:aec#purpose): owner amendment of the purpose to three capacities (Zach, 20:02 CT; relay-kit-private DEC-079). Older records that serve AEC-P0@1 or AEC-R3@1 are not re-pointed; that is Zach's call.
{"id": "AEC-P0", "version": 2, "type": "purpose", "subject": "aec-purpose", "epistemic": "committed", "owner": "AU-zach", "text": "Keep why something is built attached to what gets built in AI-assisted development, measurably, so conclusions that stop being justified are caught and legitimate revisions are kept distinct; in three capacities: Spec Kit compatibility (an extension to spec-driven development with Spec Kit); extension of other agentic coding systems (Claude Code hooks, git hooks, CI, rules files); and a standalone capacity (records, check and impact with no host framework)", "quote": "Amend Telosmith's purpose to include Spec Kit Compatibility, Extension of other Agentic Coding Systems, and a Standalone capacity.", "origin": "Zach, Claude cowork session 01GZK2KncnZ4v7e6ZAQ4C1ZH, 2026-11-04 20:02 CT", "rationale": "Owner amendment of AEC-P0@1, which described Telosmith only as an extension to Spec Kit while the primary evaluation will run in an agentic coding framework without Spec Kit (relay-kit-private CH-018, DEC-069, resolved by DEC-079). The rest of P0@1 is kept unchanged; the three capacities are Zach's terms, the examples in parentheses follow docs/use-cases.md and docs/integrations/without-spec-kit.md (PR #54).", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-P0@1"}], "anchors": [{"root": "relay-kit-private", "path": "governance/decisions.jsonl", "sha256": "95fc51d31dbef5ce1cc09347771a0abccafde2ce9783a1da4571192fe11a8444", "locator": "q:\"id\": \"DEC-079\"", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R3", "version": 2, "type": "requirement", "subject": "aec-purpose", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "Adoption is earned against a well-configured baseline for the setup in use, with authoring cost counted; if equal, simplify Telosmith. Spec Kit is one supported setup, where the baseline is a well-configured Spec Kit; in another agentic coding system the baseline is that system well configured without Telosmith, and standalone it is the same work without Telosmith", "rationale": "Follows from AEC-P0@2: with three capacities Spec Kit can no longer be the only baseline. Only the baseline clause changed; authoring cost and 'if equal, simplify' are kept. The non-Spec-Kit baseline wording is the lane builder's reading of DEC-079 ('AEC-R3 no longer makes Spec Kit the baseline'), not Zach's words; he may reword it.", "quote": "Amend Telosmith's purpose to include Spec Kit Compatibility, Extension of other Agentic Coding Systems, and a Standalone capacity.", "origin": "Zach, Claude cowork session 01GZK2KncnZ4v7e6ZAQ4C1ZH, 2026-11-04 20:02 CT", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R3@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-P0@2"}], "anchors": [{"root": "relay-kit-private", "path": "governance/decisions.jsonl", "sha256": "95fc51d31dbef5ce1cc09347771a0abccafde2ce9783a1da4571192fe11a8444", "locator": "q:\"id\": \"DEC-079\"", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "CL-R7-init", "version": 2, "type": "claim", "tier": "candidate", "claim_category": "requirement_satisfaction", "subject": "aec-scope", "text": "init still writes only absent files: it writes .aec/.gitignore (git-ignoring the generated snapshot and the hook baseline) and keeps an existing one. Its CI snippet installs the commit this aec was installed from when that is known; otherwise the release tag when the version is v0.5.0 or later; otherwise main, under a WARNING: UNPINNED comment. It never pins a release older than v0.5.0, which lacks the delivery commands", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R7@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "code:src.aec.init.init"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "code:src.aec.init.install_ref"}, {"rel": "supersedes", "to": "CL-R7-init@1"}]}
// 2026-11-04 fix/ruff-b018-records-location reconcile (claude:aec#reconcile): after merging main (#55), CL-R7-init@2 omits the source-checkout tier that resolve_install_ref() added, so version 3 states the current order. Requested by Zach (reconcile #52 with main); candidate, not owner-accepted.
{"id": "CL-R7-init", "version": 3, "type": "claim", "tier": "candidate", "claim_category": "requirement_satisfaction", "subject": "aec-scope", "text": "init still writes only absent files: it writes .aec/.gitignore (git-ignoring the generated snapshot and the hook baseline) and keeps an existing one. Its CI snippet installs, in order: the commit this aec was installed from when that is known; otherwise, when aec runs from a git checkout of Telosmith (PYTHONPATH=src or an editable install), that checkout's HEAD commit, with a note to push it or swap in a checked release tag (and a further note when aec/ has uncommitted changes); otherwise the release tag when the version is v0.5.0 or later; otherwise main, under a WARNING: UNPINNED comment. It never pins a release older than v0.5.0, which lacks the delivery commands", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R7@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "code:src.aec.init.init"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "code:src.aec.init.install_ref"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "code:src.aec.init.resolve_install_ref"}, {"rel": "supersedes", "to": "CL-R7-init@2"}]}
{"id": "EXP-dec021-fathom-replay", "version": 1, "type": "experiment", "subject": "aec-scope", "status": "pre-registered", "text": "DEC-021 replay, pre-registered and not run: three arms (conventional Spec Kit with same-fact notes and a path reminder; minimal Telosmith per the C-03 ontology audit; full Telosmith) review the real Fathom PR #15 diff 944f82f..3367ab3 from frozen revision 68890bf, 4 replicates each, plus a decoy PR at 2 each. Primary outcome: did the reviewer surface Copilot item F01 (log-box n and small-group caution counted from all complete values, not the plotted positive ones) with request-changes and a repair, graded blind against a frozen executable key. A null result lowers the priority of building on records and code-impact (DEC-032); it is not a decision to discontinue.", "rationale": "DEC-031 (Zach, 2026-11-01 21:19 CT) makes the bounded DEC-021 evaluation the next main piece of AEC work; DEC-048 (2026-11-04 09:17 CT) lets the coordinator begin it, with Kate's amendments: freeze the Fathom revision and the protocol before the replay, evaluators blind to outcomes, separate independent review. Running the replay and any contested choice of the injected change remain Zach's decisions.", "origin": "claude:aec-eval#01GZK2KncnZ4v7e6ZAQ4C1ZH, 2026-11-04, under DEC-031 and DEC-048 (canonical in relay-kit-private governance/decisions.jsonl)", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "DEC-021@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "AMB-adopted-by-others@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-P0@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-R3@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "docs/evaluations/dec-021-protocol.md", "sha256": "182486c05331c7df1c65fc3b99879d4586c66f13cf5f0a45dba89fa387acd01f", "locator": "q:**Primary outcome (pre-committed, per trial on the target PR, yes/no):**", "for": "text"}, {"path": "docs/evaluations/dec-021-ontology-audit.md", "sha256": "d1b90ade5cfae160828088e3ff9fddabe9f9fe1d261638610be81e50dc593eea", "locator": "q:## Result: the minimal set (arm B)", "for": "text"}]}
// 2026-11-04 claude:aec-eval: DEC-021 pre-registration revision 2 after two independent reviews (PR #50); still pre-registered, not frozen, not run.
{"id": "EXP-dec021-fathom-replay", "version": 2, "type": "experiment", "subject": "aec-scope", "status": "pre-registered", "text": "DEC-021 replay, revision 2, pre-registered and not run, not frozen: three arms (conventional Spec Kit; minimal Telosmith per the C-03 audit; full Telosmith) review the real Fathom PR #15 diff 3b89d7c..3367ab3. All arms get one identical prose rendering of every record and relation; B and C add Telosmith-form records and computed reports (unequal by design; parity manifest machine-checked). Precondition P1 (code-impact names FT-R7@2 or FT-R18@1) was run before any trial at 906e8fd and PR #51 and fails, so the replay measures presentation of a pointer A also receives, not code-impact's reach. Staged design: 3 A trials (stop on ceiling >=2/3), then 3 per arm, then a 4th only where undecided; >=2 is a descriptive heuristic; a tie is inconclusive; only a ceiling or the stated futility pattern is the DEC-032 null; a chance A-ahead never removes code-impact. 8M cap kept with equal-n blocks.", "rationale": "Revision after two independent reviews of revision 1 (Kate, GPT-6 High: freeze after fixes; cold Claude reviewer: limited redesign), both 2026-11-04, under DEC-031 and DEC-048. Running the replay, the cap and any contested choice of the injected change remain Zach's decisions.", "origin": "claude:aec-eval#01GZK2KncnZ4v7e6ZAQ4C1ZH, 2026-11-04, under DEC-031 and DEC-048 (canonical in relay-kit-private governance/decisions.jsonl)", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "EXP-dec021-fathom-replay@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "DEC-021@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "AMB-adopted-by-others@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-P0@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-R3@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "docs/evaluations/dec-021-protocol.md", "sha256": "20630d0dccbb13df2c3f5b00f884c78949508f62737bc2b097b462f93efdc532", "locator": "q:**Precondition P1, verbatim:**", "for": "text"}, {"path": "docs/evaluations/dec-021-ontology-audit.md", "sha256": "9138e0603b614c8d9a9daf459df774b3488e2392603ddf964f3db744a2188e9d", "locator": "q:## Result: the minimal set (arm B)", "for": "text"}, {"path": "docs/evaluations/dec-021-parity/manifest.tsv", "sha256": "19e1d59a4a8e8fd436a3bc816a465bf6867b1302fce8e7270785ee9d42cec23f", "locator": "q:kind\tfrom\trel", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-adoption", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "aec-scope", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Adopting Telosmith in another repository needs no hand-hashing and no hand-editing of the purpose stub: init takes the purpose (and a cited passage) directly, writes the hook and CI only where there is Python code, and aec append adds a record with computed anchors, refusing duplicates and records check would reject", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-P0@2"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:src.aec.init.init"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:src.aec.append.build"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:src.aec.append.make_anchor"}], "anchors": [{"path": "governance/decisions.jsonl", "sha256": "5624a3ccb4519e9a79511f91f655458d7066940b8614520ab6a859d437e7046d", "locator": "q:\"id\": \"DEC-095\"", "for": "rationale", "root": "relay-kit-private", "prefix_bytes": 94205}]}
{"id": "CL-R-adoption", "version": 1, "type": "claim", "tier": "candidate", "claim_category": "requirement_satisfaction", "subject": "aec-scope", "text": "init --purpose/--purpose-anchor, the no-code hook rule (with --hooks/--no-hooks) and aec append behave as AEC-R-adoption@1 states, including refusal without writing", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-adoption@1"}]}
{"id": "EV-R-adoption-tests", "version": 1, "type": "evidence", "tier": "candidate", "evidence_kind": "contract_conformance", "text": "tests/test_adoption_friction.py: 22 tests (written first, 19 failing before the change), covering a no-code repo, --hooks/--no-hooks, purpose text and a verified purpose anchor, refusal of a bad anchor with nothing written, and aec append: computed and alias-root anchors, prefix_bytes for append-only files, duplicate and check-rejected records refused byte-for-byte, dry run, stdin and missing final newline. Full suite 292 passed, 1 skipped", "relations": [{"rel": "supports", "to": "CL-R-adoption@1"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-adoption", "version": 2, "type": "requirement", "subject": "aec-scope", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Adopting Telosmith in another repository needs no hand-hashing and no hand-editing of the purpose stub: init takes the purpose (and a cited passage) directly, writes the hook and CI only where there is Python code, and names the CI workflow as asked (default aec); aec anchor prints a checked anchor and aec append adds a record with computed anchors, refusing duplicates and records check would reject. Adopters cite outside decisions (a private ledger) as text only. Scope from handoff HO-AEC-20261105-PPPP", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-P0@2"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:src.aec.init.init"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:src.aec.append.build"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:src.aec.append.make_anchor"}, {"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R-adoption@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "governance/decisions.jsonl", "sha256": "5624a3ccb4519e9a79511f91f655458d7066940b8614520ab6a859d437e7046d", "locator": "q:\"id\": \"DEC-095\"", "for": "rationale", "root": "relay-kit-private", "prefix_bytes": 94205}]}
{"id": "CL-R-adoption", "version": 2, "type": "claim", "tier": "candidate", "claim_category": "requirement_satisfaction", "subject": "aec-scope", "text": "init --purpose/--purpose-anchor/--ci-name, the no-code hook rule (with --hooks/--no-hooks), aec anchor and aec append behave as AEC-R-adoption@2 states, including refusal without writing", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-adoption@2"}, {"rel": "supersedes", "to": "CL-R-adoption@1"}]}
{"id": "EV-R-adoption-tests", "version": 2, "type": "evidence", "tier": "candidate", "evidence_kind": "contract_conformance", "text": "tests/test_adoption_friction.py: 30 tests, each group written first and failing before its change (19 of 22, then 7 of 8): no-code repo, --hooks/--no-hooks, purpose text and a verified purpose anchor, refusal with nothing written, --ci-name default/custom/invalid, aec anchor (checked, rationale, unresolved, outside the repo), and aec append (computed and alias-root anchors, prefix_bytes, duplicate and check-rejected records refused byte-for-byte, dry run, stdin, missing final newline). Full suite 300 passed, 1 skipped", "relations": [{"rel": "supports", "to": "CL-R-adoption@2"}, {"rel": "supersedes", "to": "EV-R-adoption-tests@1"}]}
